# Senior Living & Retirement Community Analytics – India

A portfolio project that demonstrates an end-to-end data analytics platform for a hypothetical Indian senior-living operator.

> **Important:** All data in this repository is synthetic and created for educational/portfolio purposes. It is not Chartwell data and does not represent any real retirement community.

## Business Problem

A senior-living organization operates communities across Indian cities and needs visibility into:
- Occupancy and available units
- Resident demographics and length of stay
- Service utilization and costs
- Payment status and revenue
- Property-level performance

## Architecture

```text
Synthetic CSV Data
       |
       v
Python ETL / Data Validation
       |
       v
PostgreSQL Data Warehouse
       |
       v
Star Schema / SQL Analytics
       |
       v
Power BI Dashboard
```

## Repository Structure

```text
data/       Synthetic source data
src/        Python ingestion, validation and KPI calculations
sql/        PostgreSQL schema and analytical queries
docs/       Dashboard and architecture notes
```

## Technology Stack

- Python / Pandas
- PostgreSQL
- SQL
- Power BI
- Git/GitHub

## Key KPIs

### Occupancy
- Occupancy %
- Occupied units
- Available units
- Occupancy by property and city

### Resident
- Resident count
- Average age
- Care level distribution
- Length of stay

### Services
- Service volume
- Service cost
- Cost by service type

### Payments
- Total billed amount
- Paid / pending / overdue amount
- Collection rate

## How to Run

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
python src/validate_data.py
python src/kpi_analysis.py
```

## Suggested Power BI Pages

1. Executive Overview
2. Occupancy & Property Performance
3. Resident Analytics
4. Services & Payments

## Future Enhancements

- Load the data into Azure Data Lake or AWS S3
- Build an automated ETL pipeline
- Add incremental loading
- Add data-quality audit tables
- Create a PostgreSQL/Snowflake dimensional warehouse
- Add occupancy forecasting with Python
- Add Power BI row-level security
